id: dangerous
name: Dangerous
kind: battlefield
envQuality: true
groundCollision: doubles
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Ground that bites back. Twice the Collision Damage from hitting it.
text: >
  Dangerous: Double any Collision Damage you receive from this Environment.

---

# The shortest Quality and the meanest. `groundCollision: doubles`, read by the collision
# window in its Ground Collision branch.
#
# "From this Environment", so it is the ground and not a Feature standing on it - the same
# line every Quality here is drawn on.
#
# It doubles the way the Launching Profile doubles, which means the two multiply rather than
# stacking: a Dangerous Square under a Launching attack is four times what the Rank is
# worth. Both are settled in the one multiply that already holds every doubling and
# halving, so the arithmetic is the same arithmetic.
#
# No statements. A collision is an event.
